tle\":\"www.tiktokshop.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.tiktokshop.com/pdp/cayenne-pepper-softgels-supplement-supports-circulation/1731315079510725077\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a full ingredient list for the Aurivita Cayenne Pepper softgel with 10 supporting botanicals, so I can't confirm that exact lineup.\n\n- **Brand and product:** Aurivita is run by Azeal Supplements LLC and describes itself as focused on cardiovascular health. The company says it is a brand owned and operated by Azeal Supplements LLC. Its flagship, Capsaicin Power, is described as a cayenne blend with hawthorn, beetroot, turmeric, ginseng, and other ingredients. The company's flagship product, Aurivita Capsaicin Power, combines cayenne pepper with hawthorn, beetroot, turmeric, ginseng, and more.\n- **Softgel format:** The brand's softgel is pitched as a way to get cayenne without its burn. It is formulated as an easy-to-swallow softgel for people who want cayenne without the burn of raw peppers.\n- **Similar-looking listings:** A TikTok Shop listing describes a softgel with cayenne, hawthorn, beets, turmeric, vitamin D3+K2, vitamin E, grape seed, and ginseng. It lists cayenne pepper organic, hawthorn berry, beets, turmeric, vitamin D3 and K2, vitamin E, grape seed oil, and ginseng. The listing doesn't name Aurivita, so I can't tie it to this product.\n- **Reviews are mixed:** Trustpilot shows a score of about 4.4 to 4.5 out of 5, though the figures on different pages vary. Some reviewers praise the product, while others allege counterfeits. One 1-star reviewer says they received counterfeit product from Aurivita.co after ordering the cayenne pepper softgels directly from the site. Another reviewer reports no detectable heat from the softgel. These are unverified individual accounts.\n\nTo verify the actual ingredient list, check the supplement facts panel on Aurivita's official site or the bottle, or ask the company directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response 