-1-cayenne-as-a-curative/3/) A HealthUnlocked poster said the approach worked for them some of the time, but not every time. [healthunlocked.com](https://healthunlocked.com/sruk/posts/823918/cure-with-cayenne)\n- **Supplement and wellness sites promote it.** Naturally Savvy recommends cayenne capsules taken before cold exposure as its top pick for cold extremities. [naturallysavvy.com](https://naturallysavvy.com/blog/cold-hands-and-feet) A Substack naturopath says a pinch of cayenne before going out can keep hands and feet warm. [substack.com](https://izzyseadon.substack.com/p/cold-hands-warm-heartcold-feet-neglected) Some of these pages are selling products or courses, so treat them with caution.\n- **Evidence is thin.** One explainer describes the warming effect as anecdotal and historical, not clinically proven. [ntro.it.com](https://ntro.it.com/does-cayenne-pepper-increase-circulation) MSK's patient page notes only that cayenne is used in traditional medicine for circulation. [mskcc.org](https://www.mskcc.org/pdf/cancer-care/patient-education/herbs/cayenne)\n- **Cold hands and feet can have medical causes.** Raynaud's, thyroid problems, and some medications can all cause them, and one AARP thread notes that beta-blockers and stimulants like Sudafed can reduce blood flow to the extremities. [community.aarp.org](https://community.aarp.org/t5/Healthy-Living/Cold-hands-amp-feet-from-medicines/m-p/2348562) Talking to a doctor first is sensible, especially if the symptoms are new or one-sided, or if there is color change or pain."],"durationSeconds":7.992530750000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0182ssWPBaLivcYqevTgpJCs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017QakMd6QtRstJvfy1iQov2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"capsaicin cayenne supplement side effects interactions anticoagulants blood pressure medication\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"www.mskcc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.mskcc.org/node/3219\"},{\"title\":\"Common Names\",\"url\":\"https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/herb/cayenne\"},{\"title\":\"nlm.nih.gov\",\"url\":\"https://nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/druginfo/natural/945.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.mskcc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/integrative-medicine/herbs/cayenne\"},{\"title\":\"www.webmd.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.webmd.com/vitamins-supplements/capsicum?print=true\"},{\"title\":\"www.webmd.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.webmd.com/vitamins-supplements/capsicum\"},{\"title\":\"Possible Interactions with: Cayenne\",\"url\":\"https://stlukes-stl.com/health-content/medicine/33/000885.htm\"},{\"title\":\"Cayenne Pepper and Warfarin\",\"url\":\"https://www.livestrong.com/article/527304-cayenne-pepper-and-warfarin/\"},{\"title\":\"Key takeaways\",\"url\":\"https://www.singlecare.com/blog/?p=627786\"},{\"title\":\"www.mskcc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.mskcc.org/pdf/cancer-care/patient-education/herbs/cayenne\"}]\n\nThe search turned up consistent warnings on the three areas you asked about, though the strength of the evidence varies by source.\n\n**Blood thinners (anticoagulants):** This is the interaction sources treat most seriously. One source says capsaicin may increase bleeding risk with warfarin and heparin, and lists herbs like ginkgo and garlic as similar concerns (Blood-thinning medications and herbs -- Capsaicin may increase the risk of bleeding associated with certain blood-thinning medications (such as warfarin and heparin)). Another notes that cayenne can further increase the risk of bleeding, as capsaicin may reduce blood clotting. The MSKCC herb monograph, however, says the antiplatelet effect seen in animal models has yet to be determined clinically.\n\n**Blood pressure:** Sources disagree. MedlinePlus says taking capsicum or eating a large amount of chili peppers might cause a spike in blood pressure. In theory, this might worsen the condition for people who already have high blood pressure. MSKCC notes that a systematic review found no impact on blood pressure or heart rate. MSKCC also advises talking to a provider first if you have high blood pressure or heart conditions.\n\n**Blood pressure medications (ACE inhibitors):** The main concern is cough. Capsaicin cream may increase the cough that some ACE inhibitors cause, but MedlinePlus says it isn't clear if this interaction is a big concern. One source describes ACE inhibitor interactions as rare and unlikely.\n\n**Other notable interactions:** Diabetes medications and blood-sugar-lowering supplements may cause blood sugar to drop too low (Cayenne can lower your blood sugar too much if you take it with a diabetes medication). Ciprofloxacin and theophylline absorption may also increase.\n\n**Side effects:** Common ones are stomach irritation, sweating, and eye or nose irritation. Supplements are not standardized, so potency varies by brand (The FDA has not tested capsicum products to confirm that they contain the ingredients or amounts stated on their labels.).\n\n**Bottom line:** Talk with a doctor or pharmacist before taking cayenne or capsaicin supplements if you take warfarin, heparin, other anticoagulants, diabetes medication, or blood pressure medication, or if you have high blood pressure or heart disease. The bleeding interaction with blood thinners is the most important one to discuss.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ae1b95f-0a75-4473-b2e5-cff7fb3dca41","uuid":"1f64727c-1a8c-4d3b-ad49-25674522aaf8","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:00:54.479Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"capsaicin cayenne supplement side effects interactions anticoagulants blood pressure medication","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014ZufKdHLEHW9K6AJPDsR4w","content":[{"title":"www.mskcc.org","url":"https://www.mskcc.org/node/3219"},{"title":"Common Names","url":"https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/herb/cayenne"},{"title":"nlm.nih.gov","url":"https://nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/druginfo/natural/945.html"},{"title":"www.mskcc.org","url":"https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/integrative-medicine/herbs/cayenne"},{"title":"www.webmd.com","url":"https://www.webmd.com/vitamins-supplements/capsicum?print=true"},{"title":"www.webmd.com","url":"https://www.webmd.com/vitamins-supplements/capsicum"},{"title":"Possible Interactions with: Cayenne","url":"https://stlukes-stl.com/health-content/medicine/33/000885.htm"},{"title":"Cayenne Pepper and Warfarin","url":"https://www.livestrong.com/article/527304-cayenne-pepper-and-warfarin/"},{"title":"Key takeaways","url":"https://www.singlecare.com/blog/?p=627786"},{"title":"www.mskcc.org","url":"https://www.mskcc.org/pdf/cancer-care/patient-education/herbs/cayenne"}]},"The search turned up consistent warnings on the three areas you asked about, though the strength of the evidence varies by source.\n\n**Blood thinners (anticoagulants):** This is the interaction sources treat most seriously. One source says capsaicin may increase bleeding risk with warfarin and heparin, and lists herbs like ginkgo and garlic as similar concerns (Blood-thinning medications and herbs -- Capsaicin may increase the risk of bleeding associated with certain blood-thinning medications (such as warfarin and heparin)). Another notes that cayenne can further increase the risk of bleeding, as capsaicin may reduce blood clotting. The MSKCC herb monograph, however, says the antiplatelet effect seen in animal models has yet to be determined clinically.\n\n**Blood pressure:** Sources disagree. MedlinePlus says taking capsicum or eating a large amount of chili peppers might cause a spike in blood pressure. In theory, this might worsen the condition for people who already have high blood pressure. MSKCC notes that a systematic review found no impact on blood pressure or heart rate. MSKCC also advises talking to a provider first if you have high blood pressure or heart conditions.\n\n**Blood pressure medications (ACE inhibitors):** The main concern is cough. Capsaicin cream may increase the cough that some ACE inhibitors cause, but MedlinePlus says it isn't clear if this interaction is a big concern. One source describes ACE inhibitor interactions as rare and unlikely.\n\n**Other notable interactions:** Diabetes medications and blood-sugar-lowering supplements may cause blood sugar to drop too low (Cayenne can lower your blood sugar too much if you take it with a diabetes medication). Ciprofloxacin and theophylline absorption may also increase.\n\n**Side effects:** Common ones are stomach irritation, sweating, and eye or nose irritation. Supplements are not standardized, so potency varies by brand (The FDA has not tested capsicum products to confirm that they contain the ingredients or amounts stated on their labels.).\n\n**Bottom line:** Talk with a doctor or pharmacist before taking cayenne or capsaicin supplements if you take warfarin, heparin, other anticoagulants, diabetes medication, or blood pressure medication, or if you have high blood pressure or heart disease. The bleeding interaction with blood thinners is the most important one to discuss."],"durationSeconds":8.263136125,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017QakMd6QtRstJvfy1iQov2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNpSztEhUpUd87QhUSfeLz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Colombia enfermedades cardiovasculares hipertensión cifras 2025 Ministerio de Salud\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Estilo de Vida\",\"url\":\"https://www.publimetro.co/estilo-vida/2025/09/19/dia-mundial-del-corazon-cada-dia-mueren-219-colombianos-por-enfermedad-cardiovascular/\"},{\"title\":\"proesa pb16 esp\",\"url\":\"https://www.icesi.edu.co/proesa/images/publicaciones/politicas-en-breve/pdf/proesa-pb16_esp.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Reporte SCV Quibdo vf\",\"url\":\"https://gobierno.uniandes.edu.co/wp-content/uploads/Reporte-SCV-Quibdo-vf.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Mortalidad por riesgo cardiovascular se redujo un 29 % en Colombia\",\"url\":\"https://www.noticiasrcn.com/salud/mortalidad-por-riesgo-cardiovascular-se-redujo-un-29-en-colombia-393511\"},{\"title\":\"PROESA dt34\",\"url\":\"https://www.icesi.edu.co/proesa/images/publicaciones/documentos-de-trabajo/pdf/PROESA_dt34.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Siete millones de colombianos enfrentan riesgo cardiovascular: avance, brechas y prioridades de gestión para 2026\",\"url\":\"https://consultorsalud.com/riesgo-cardiovascular-colombia-millones-hta-d/\"},{\"title\":\"Pico y Placa Medellín\",\"url\":\"https://www.elcolombiano.com/tendencias/enfermedades-cardiovasculares-estudio-demuestra-aumento-EK29452116\"},{\"title\":\"lineamientos gestion enfermedades cardiovasculares metabolicas\",\"url\":\"https://www.minsalud.gov.co/sites/rid/Lists/BibliotecaDigital/RIDE/VS/PP/ENT/lineamientos-gestion-enfermedades-cardiovasculares-metabolicas.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"La importancia de controlar la tensión arterial para iniciar un año sin riesgos graves para la salud\",\"url\":\"https://www.noticiasrcn.com/salud-y-bienestar/importancia-de-controlar-la-tension-arterial-para-iniciar-un-ano-sin-riesgos-graves-para-la-salud-990675\"},{\"title\":\"Siete millones de colombianos enfrentan riesgo cardiovascular: avance, brechas y prioridades de gestión para 2026\",\"url\":\"https://consultorsalud.com/?p=343777\"},{\"title\":\"tres enfermedades lideran las estadisticas en colombia y van en aumento 636980\",\"url\":\"https://www.portafolio.co/tendencias/sociales/tres-enfermedades-lideran-las-estadisticas-en-colombia-y-van-en-aumento-636980\"},{\"title\":\"proesa pb 12\",\"url\":\"https://icesi.edu.co/proesa/images/publicaciones/politicas-en-breve/pdf/proesa-pb-12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"las promesas que le debe hacer su corazon 548060\",\"url\":\"https://www.elheraldo.co/salud/las-promesas-que-le-debe-hacer-su-corazon-548060\"},{\"title\":\"plan escalamiento iniciativa hearts colombia junio\",\"url\":\"https://paho.org/sites/default/files/2021-08/plan-escalamiento-iniciativa-hearts-colombia-junio.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Enfermedades cardiovasculares en Colombia: siguen siendo la principal causa de muerte\",\"url\":\"https://canaltrece.com.co/noticias/enfermedades-cardiovasculares-en-colombia/\"},{\"title\":\"gpc actualizacion parcial hta primaria vps\",\"url\":\"https://www.minsalud.gov.co/sites/rid/Lists/BibliotecaDigital/RIDE/DE/CA/gpc-actualizacion-parcial-hta-primaria-vps.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Día Mundial del ACV: Colombia registró 17.037 muertes por enfermedades cerebrovasculares en 2025\",\"url\":\"https://consultorsalud.com/?p=346081\"},{\"title\":\"Sep 29, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.novartis.com/co-es/news/media-releases/controlar-el-colesterol-ldl-en-colombia-la-clave-para-salvar-miles-de-vidas-y-optimizar-el-gasto-en-salud\"},{\"title\":\"colombia registro un aumento del 35 en muertes por enfermedades cardiovasculares durante el ultimo ano\",\"url\":\"https://www.infobae.com/colombia/2023/09/29/colombia-registro-un-aumento-del-35-en-muertes-por-enfermedades-cardiovasculares-durante-el-ultimo-ano/\"}]\n\nLos resultados dan un panorama bastante completo, aunque las cifras no siempre coinciden y ninguna proviene directamente de un informe 2025 del Ministerio de Salud.\n\n- **Mortalidad:** Un artículo de Publimetro atribuye al Ministerio de Salud y al DANE más de 80.000 muertes anuales por enfermedades cardiovasculares, unas 219 al día (más de 80.000 personas mueren anualmente en Colombia a causa de enfermedades cardiovasculares, lo que equivale a 219 fallecimientos diarios). Un documento de PROESA de 2026 cita al DANE para 2025: las enfermedades isquémicas del corazón fueron la principal causa de muerte, con 92,7 por cada 100.000 habitantes (92.7 muertes por 100.000 habitantes).\n- **Hipertensión:** Según la Cuenta de Alto Costo, hubo 6.703.467 casos prevalentes de hipertensión entre julio de 2024 y junio de 2025 (). PROESA, citando a la CAC, indica que la prevalencia subió de 7,6 % en 2017 a 11,9 % en 2024 ().\n- **Ministerio de Salud:** Según una nota de RCN, el Ministerio reportó más de 5 millones de personas diagnosticadas con hipertensión en 2024, y estima que una cantidad similar la padece sin saberlo ().\n- **Riesgo combinado:** El reporte 2025 de la Cuenta de Alto Costo registra 7.074.181 personas con al menos una de tres condiciones: hipertensión, diabetes tipo 2 o enfermedad renal crónica ().\n- **Cerebrovasculares:** El DANE registró 17.037 defunciones por enfermedades cerebrovasculares en 2025, equivalentes al 6,0 % de las muertes no fetales del país ().\n- **Guía clínica:** El Ministerio publicó en 2025 una actualización parcial de su guía de práctica clínica para la hipertensión arterial primaria (Guía 18) ().\n\nConviene verificar las cifras de muertes contra los boletines oficiales del DANE antes de citarlas. Las fuentes de prensa mezclan periodos y definiciones, y la cifra de 80.000 muertes no coincide con los datos de tasa por habitante citados por PROESA.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ae1b95f-0a75-4473-b2e5-cff7fb3dca41","uuid":"d8174aa8-9078-42a2-a7fb-d156fcce3112","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14: