he TikTok Shop reviews are thin and mostly anecdotal. I found no independent evidence on circulation benefits.\n\n- **Same formula, multiple sellers:** A 240-count softgel is listed on TikTok Shop by ForestWell, with a 4.9 rating from 16 reviews and 299 sold. It is listed as a cayenne softgel for circulation and vitality with vitamin D3, K2, beetroot and hawthorn extracts. A second TikTok listing from VIVONU, with a 4.4 rating from about 3.2k reviews and 47.3K sold, is marked as a 12-in-1 blend that includes ginseng. A third, from CellJuvMax, is also a 240-capsule 12-in-1 product sold by a different seller. Walmart carries a 240-softgel BFQN version with the same core ingredients.\n- **Marketing claims:** The listings say the product supports leg vein, heart and blood vessel health. The TikTok copy does not cite clinical trials.\n- **Review quality:** The ForestWell reviews are brief, anecdotal and one-sided, such as a user saying their joint pain has eased. The CellJuvMax listing has one review, which complains that the product was made in China. The VIVONU rating is the strongest signal, but I could not verify whether the reviews are genuine or how many are verified purchases.\n- **Ingredient caveat:** Swanson's cayenne capsules, which are a different product, do list hawthorn and ginger, and their sourcing and dosing differ from the softgels above. Dosing and sourcing details for the softgels are not consistent across listings, so compare the supplement facts panel directly.\n\nIf you're assessing a specific listing, the key checks are the seller's identity, whether the reviews are verified, and whether the label gives doses for each ingredient.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ae1b95f-0a75-4473-b2e5-cff7fb3dca41","uuid":"1812d41f-87a0-4693-8c28-63ae9aded5f3","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:01:22.077Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"cayenne pepper softgel